  "lineage": "Somali qaraami art-song tradition emerging in 1940s Mogadishu and Hargeisa as urban-classical Somali popular music, incorporating Arabian peninsular oud and qanun with Somali-language poetic-meter. The genre matured through the Somali Republic golden-age 1960s-1970s with Radio Mogadishu broadcasting the canonical Hargeisa-school singers. Vocal style features melismatic ornament over Arabic maqam vocabulary with Somali-Cushitic vocal-inflection. The post-1991 civil war disrupted institutional transmission; diaspora-revival in Minneapolis, London, and Toronto sustains contemporary practice.",
